US-046 complete and committed (`18bf257`). Implemented the CodeCloze widget end-to-end: Zod schema with discriminated `validation` (exact / regex / oneOf), optional `finalTests` and progressive `hints`; React widget that splits the template on `{{slotId}}` markers, renders surrounding code via a small regex-based Python tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-calls), and renders each slot as a content-sized inline `<input>` (min 60 px) with green/red border on blur — wrong answers reveal the per-slot hint inline and bump a global counter that progressively unfurls `hints[].markdown`; once every slot is correct, Submit runs the `finalTests` through the existing `usePyodide().runWithTests` (test isolation per US-031) and PATCHes `/api/progress` with `{ done: true }` on pass. Editor follows the US-023 pattern: textarea for `taskMarkdown`, CodeMirror Python pane for `template`, slots list with id/hint/validation kind+value selector, expandable test bodies, hints list, sources field; full Zod safeParse + dirty/error surfacing. Wired the `--widget-code-cloze` CSS var (light + dark), a `widgetRegistry.codeCloze` entry (PenLine icon), the `WidgetType` union, the `CodeClozeSectionSchema` variant, the `WidgetEditPanel` + `SectionRenderer` branches, and added `code-cloze` to `npm run build:schemas`. Added 5 Vitest blocks (51/51 schemas-suite tests pass) covering minimal-valid parse, finalTests/hints/per-slot-hint, unknown-kind reject, empty-oneOf reject, plus `validateSlotValue` exact/oneOf/regex (anchored full-match, invalid-pattern returns false). Verified in playwright headless on `cloze-test/box-blur`: filling `aggregator` with the wrong "avg" turned the slot red and rendered both the inline `slot.hint` and progressive hint #0; fixing it to "sum" turned it green; filling `divisor` with "len(values)" turned the second slot green; once Pyodide reached `ready` the Submit button enabled, both finalTests passed, the button morphed to "Solved", server-side `GET /api/progress` confirmed `sectionState.c1.done === true`, and on a fresh load the section's `data-status="done"` badge rendered.
